{"id": "86166", "name": "כפל שברים אלגבריים – חזקות של x ו-y (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Simplify the following:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}\\cdot{{CT:1}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Leave your answer as a single fraction in its simplest form.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">= [[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Multiply the numerators and the denominators, then combine the powers of the same base.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Multiply numerators and denominators</b><br>When multiplying algebraic fractions use the same method as for normal fractions. Multiply the numerators and the denominators together to get the numerator and denominator of the answer:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}\\cdot{{CT:1}}=\\frac{{{CT:2}}\\cdot {{CT:3}}}{{{CT:4}}\\cdot {{CT:5}}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Laws of exponents</b><br>In the numerator use <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(a^m\\cdot a^n=a^{m+n}\\)</span>: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x^{{CT:6}}\\cdot x^{{CT:7}}=x^{{CT:8}}\\)</span>. Be sure to reduce the fraction to its lowest terms: here nothing cancels, because the numerator has only the factor <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x\\)</span> and the denominator has only a number and powers of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(y\\)</span>. In this example:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}\\cdot{{CT:1}} = \\frac{{CT:9}}{{CT:10}} = {{CT:11}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": false, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is algebraically equivalent to the correct answer but is not in its simplest form.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "pa", "pc", "ps", "ta", "v"], "nvariants": 50}